// requestUserFeedback -- ask the user for missing detail mid-task
// ================================================================
//
// First-class, agent-facing way to pause the active Plan and ask the
// user a question when the agent (or a specialist it is fronting for)
// is missing the information needed to continue. Before this tool the
// awaitingFeedback / feedback_required path was PLANNER-decided only:
// the planner agent loop's escalateAwaitingFeedback transitioned the
// Plan when it ran out of road. The agent itself had no way to raise
// its hand mid-turn.
//
// The handler:
//
//   1. Transitions the active Plan (planId is auto-stamped from the
//      turn context -- the agent never has to know its own Plan id)
//      to status=awaitingFeedback / feedbackReason=feedback_required.
//
//   2. Writes the feedbackRequest object the canvas card renders:
//
//        {
//          question:   string,                   -- what to ask the user
//          kind:       "choice"|"text"|"multi",  -- response widget
//          options?:   [{label, value}],         -- for choice / multi
//          askedAt:    <now>,
//          askedByTaskId?: <task id when known>,
//          timeoutAt?: <RFC3339>                 -- optional auto-pause
//        }
//
//   3. Returns a small ack payload {status:"awaiting_user", planId,
//      kind}. The agent reads it, emits a short respondToUser
//      acknowledgement, and ENDS ITS TURN. The agent's process exits
//      cleanly; the user's answer is the gate.
//
// Resume path (existing mechanism, unchanged): the user answers via
// the canvas card's per-kind response widget, which stamps
// Plan.feedbackResponse {response, respondedBy, respondedAt} and
// bumps status back to running. The planner integration's Plan-
// transition subscriber (awaitingFeedback -> running) re-invokes the
// owning agent with the persisted TaskState + feedbackResponse in
// bootstrap context.
//
// The GENERIC plan.awaitingFeedback canvas-card producer that renders
// the feedback_required variant lives in the BFF (the carrier repo's
// product pack DSL tree) and is delivered in the follow-up BFF wave;
// only the scope_elevation_required variant has a producer today.
// This tool is the memql-side half.
//
// allowedRoles: assistant. Specialists never speak to humans, so they
// surface a "needsMore" via askSpecialist and the assistant raises the
// feedback request on their behalf -- the assistant is the sole agent
// that converses with the user.

@handler(type="function", name="requestUserFeedback")
@allowedRoles("assistant")
@executionTime("fast")
@description("Pause the active Plan and ask the user for missing detail mid-task. Transitions the Plan to awaitingFeedback (feedbackReason=feedback_required) and lands a feedback card on the canvas. Use this -- not a guess -- when you (or a specialist you are fronting for) need information, a decision, or a file the user has not provided. After calling it, emit a short acknowledgement and END YOUR TURN; the user's answer resumes the Plan.")
tool requestUserFeedback {
  question     string  @required @description("The question to put to the user. Be specific and self-contained -- the user sees only this text on the card, not the chat history. State exactly what you need and why.")
  kind         string  @required @enum("choice", "text", "multi") @description("Response widget. choice = pick exactly one of `options`. multi = pick one or more of `options`. text = free-form (also the path for a file the user drops in chat/canvas). Pick choice/multi whenever the answer space is bounded -- it is faster and less error-prone for the user.")
  options      array   @description("For kind=choice / multi: the selectable answers, each an object {label, value}. label is shown to the user; value is what comes back in feedbackResponse. Omit for kind=text.")
  timeoutAt    string  @description("Optional RFC3339 deadline. When set and passed, the feedbackTimeoutAutoPause cron moves the Plan from awaitingFeedback to paused so it does not hang forever. Omit to wait indefinitely.")
  planId       string  @autoInjected @description("The active Plan to park. Server-stamped from the agent runtime turn context; the central validator drops any LLM-supplied value before dispatch (memql#107).")
  agentId      string  @autoInjected @description("Calling agent id. Server-stamped from the agent runtime; the central validator drops any LLM-supplied value before dispatch.")
  ownerUserId  string  @autoInjected @description("Session-owner user id. Server-stamped; scopes the parked Plan's owner attribution. The central validator drops any LLM-supplied value.")
  partitionId      string  @autoInjected @description("Target space for the canvas card. Server-stamped from the agent runtime; the central validator drops any LLM-supplied value.")
}
